# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
kant-practical-2.md:1: argue/readings: S4 is read 2 ways: kant-practical-2.logic.r2 has nothing from it; kant-practical-2.logic.r2.2 and kant-practical-2.logic.r2.3 have "endless_variety → ¬same_all"; they differ when only "the variety of judgement must be endless" and "the principle of happiness prescribes the same practical rules to all rational beings" are true, which the first allows
kant-practical-2.md:1: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps kant-practical-2.logic.r2.2 and kant-practical-2.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "the variety of judgement must be endless" and "the principle of happiness prescribes the same practical rules to all rational beings" are true. Is S4, "This principle, therefore, does not prescribe the same practical rules to all rational beings, although the rules are all included under a common title, namely, that of happiness.", true then?
kant-practical-2.logic.r2: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 2 ways: kant-practical-2.logic.r2 has "endless_variety → ¬same_all"; kant-practical-2.logic.r2.2 and kant-practical-2.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; they differ when only "the variety of judgement must be endless" and "the principle of happiness prescribes the same practical rules to all rational beings" are true, which the second allows
kant-practical-2.md:1: argue/readings: the conclusion is read 2 ways: kant-practical-2.logic.r2 has "¬laws"; kant-practical-2.logic.r2.2 and kant-practical-2.logic.r2.3 have "maxims ∧ ¬laws"; they differ when nothing is true, which the first allows
kant-practical-2.md:1: argue/answered: the conclusion: answered no, which keeps kant-practical-2.logic.r2.2 and kant-practical-2.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "the principle of happiness may furnish maxims" and "the principle of happiness can furnish laws of the will (practical laws can be founded on it)" are false. Is the conclusion, "The principle of happiness may, indeed, furnish maxims, but never such as would be competent to be laws of the will, even if universal happiness were made the object.", true then?
